    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0265" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/7–2244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of European
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        Admiral William D. Leahy, Chief of Staff to the Commander in Chief of the
                        Army and Navy</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-07-22">July 22, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There are enclosed two memoranda prepared in the Department of State respecting
                    the treatment of Austria and Germany, together with two summary statements to
                    accompany these memoranda setting forth policy recommendations.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d133-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>These reports were prepared at the request of the Post-War Programs Committee of
                    the Department of State and have been approved by this Committee. The two papers
                    on Austria, furthermore, have been submitted to the White House and were
                    approved by the President.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d133-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Department of State would welcome the comment of the United States Joint
                    Chiefs of Staff on these memoranda, and particularly would like to be informed
                    if the Joint Chiefs of Staff approve those sections which relate to military
                    considerations.</p>
                <pb facs="0266" n="252" xml:id="pg252"/>
                <p>After consideration by the Joint Chiefs of Staff, it is anticipated that both
                    reports will be transmitted to Ambassador Winant in London for background and
                    guidance in his discussions in the European Advisory Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ames</hi>] C. D[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">unn</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d133-f1" n="2" xml:id="d133-f1-content">
                <p>For texts of the memorandum dated June 8 and summary dated June 21 respecting the
                    treatment of Austria, see <ref target="#pg438">pp. 438</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg447">447</ref>, respectively. For texts of the memorandum dated
                    August 5 and summary dated May 31 respecting the treatment of Germany, see <ref
                        target="#pg306">pp. 306</ref> and <ref target="#pg302">302</ref>,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
